<title>SOUTH AFRICA: DISTILLERS HALF YEAR SHR RISES.</title>
<headline>DISTILLERS HALF YEAR SHR RISES.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31 </p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     73.0	  vs 58.2</p>
<p>    Cash equiv earnings (cts) 85.8    vs 69.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 21.0	  vs 17.0 </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   102.14	vs 81.53</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   171.88	vs 149.46</p>
<p>    Tax			 64.17	 vs 63.15</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,019.80    vs 829.99</p>
<p>Div payable February 28</p>
<p>on register February 21</p>
<p>Full name: Distillers Corp Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The South African drinks firm said that the wine and</p>
<p>spirt market had shown growth in the period despite a slow down</p>
<p>in economic activity.</p>
<p>However, it warned that a decline in the growth of private</p>
<p>consumption expenditure is being currently experienced. &quot;Unless</p>
<p>the decline is more than anticipated the group expects to</p>
<p>maintain the current growth in earnings for the full year,&quot; the</p>
<p>firm said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
